# GEM Template — Agent Ruleset

## Project snapshot
- **Stack**: SvelteKit 5 (Runes API), Tailwind CSS 4, shadcn-svelte, TypeScript strict
- **Adapter**: `adapter-node` → standalone Node.js server, deployed via Coolify on Hetzner VPS
- **Purpose**: Reusable trade-business landing-page template. One `config.ts` swap = new client.

---

## The cardinal rule — `src/lib/config.ts`

`config.ts` is the **single client-customisation surface**. Every piece of client identity lives
there: brand, contact, address, services, opening hours, social proof, partner names, problem
types, meta, OG.

- **Never hardcode** client-specific text, numbers, or names anywhere else in the codebase.
- **Never duplicate** config values — always import from `$lib/config`.
- When a component needs a new data field, add it to `config.ts` first, then consume it.

---

## Source of truth for UI copy — `src/lib/i18n.ts`

All user-facing strings (labels, headings, CTAs, aria-labels) live in `T.de` and `T.en` inside
`i18n.ts`. Components receive the correct locale object via `lang.svelte.ts` and read `t.section.key`.

- **Never hardcode** display strings inside `.svelte` files.
- When adding new copy, add both `de` and `en` entries in `i18n.ts` **before** touching the component.

---

## Directory contract

```
src/
├── lib/
│   ├── actions/        # Svelte actions (DOM behaviour helpers, e.g. reveal.ts)
│   ├── components/     # Chrome/shell: Navbar, Footer, LangSwitch, ThemeSwitch
│   │                   # Always rendered regardless of page — never section-specific
│   ├── ui/             # Page section components: Hero, ServiceCards, WhyUs, etc.
│   │                   # One file per content block, named after the section
│   ├── config.ts       # ← CLIENT IDENTITY — swap this per deployment
│   ├── i18n.ts         # ← ALL UI copy in de + en
│   ├── lang.svelte.ts  # Rune-based active language state
│   ├── theme.svelte.ts # Rune-based active theme state
│   ├── utils.ts        # Pure utility functions (cn helper, etc.)
│   └── index.ts        # Public re-exports for $lib
└── routes/
    ├── +layout.svelte  # JSON-LD, meta tags, Navbar/Footer shell
    ├── +page.svelte    # Home page — composes ui/ sections
    ├── +page.server.ts # Form action (WhatsApp redirect + optional Resend)
    ├── datenschutz/    # Privacy policy
    └── impressum/      # Legal notice
```

Placement rules:
- `components/` = always-on chrome. `ui/` = replaceable page sections.
- New reusable layout elements → `components/`. New page sections → `ui/`.
- New shared logic/helpers → `src/lib/` root (e.g. `animations.ts`), not scattered in subdirs.
- New routes with backend logic → `routes/[slug]/+page.server.ts` alongside the page file.
- **Do not create** a `types/`, `stores/`, or `helpers/` directory for a handful of files —
  keep types co-located with the file that owns them.

---

## Svelte 5 — Runes only

This project targets Svelte 5. The legacy Options API is **forbidden**.

| Forbidden (legacy) | Use instead (Svelte 5) |
|---|---|
| `export let prop` | `let { prop } = $props()` |
| `$: derived` | `$derived(expr)` |
| `writable()` / `readable()` stores | Rune-based state in `*.svelte.ts` files |
| `onMount` for reactive side-effects | `$effect()` |
| `<svelte:component this={C}>` | Direct component variable in markup |
| `on:click={handler}` | `onclick={handler}` |

Rune-based state modules live in `src/lib/` as `*.svelte.ts` files (e.g. `theme.svelte.ts`).

---

## TypeScript

- `strict: true` is enforced — no implicit `any`, no `!` non-null assertions without comment.
- Types shared across multiple files are defined in the file that semantically owns them
  (e.g. `Service`, `Stat`, `USP` live in `config.ts`). Do not move them to a separate `types/` file.
- Use `as const` on config objects to get literal types for free.
- All component props must be typed via `$props()` destructuring with explicit types.

---

## Styling

- **Tailwind CSS 4** utilities everywhere. No custom CSS except in `src/app.css`.
- `app.css` owns: CSS custom properties (theme tokens), font imports, base resets only.
- Class composition uses `cn()` from `$lib/utils` (clsx + tailwind-merge).
- Responsive prefix order: base → `sm:` → `md:` → `lg:` → `xl:`.
- Do not use inline `style=` attributes — use Tailwind utilities or CSS custom properties.
- Do not use `@apply` in CSS — write utilities directly in `.svelte` files.

---

## Formatting (matches `.prettierrc`)

- **Tabs** for indentation — never spaces.
- **Single quotes** for strings.
- **No trailing commas**.
- **100 character** print width.
- Run `npm run format` before every commit. CI will reject unformatted code.

---

## Imports

- Always use the `$lib/` path alias for `src/lib` imports — never relative `../../`.
- Import order: Svelte/SvelteKit internals → `$lib/` → sibling `.svelte` files.
- Do not create barrel re-exports inside `components/` or `ui/` subdirectories.
  Import each component directly: `import Hero from '$lib/ui/Hero.svelte'`.

---

## Agent roles and ownership

### Frontend Developer
- **Owns**: `src/lib/components/`, `src/lib/ui/`, `src/app.css`, `src/lib/i18n.ts`
- **May read, not modify**: `config.ts` — propose data shape changes to the Orchestrator
- **Branch prefix**: `feat/` or `fix/`

### DevOps Automator
- **Owns**: `svelte.config.js`, `vite.config.ts`, `package.json`, `.env.example`, `DEPLOY.md`,
  CI/CD config files
- **Does not touch** `src/` except to resolve build or type errors
- **Branch prefix**: `chore/` or `infra/`

### Git Workflow Master
- Enforces the branching model below
- Reviews PRs before merge to `dev` or `main`
- **Branch prefix**: `release/` or `hotfix/`

### Agents Orchestrator (Claude Code)
- Coordinates cross-cutting changes (new section = `config.ts` + `i18n.ts` + `ui/` + route)
- Has final say on directory structure and naming conventions
- **Branch prefix**: `scaffold/` or `refactor/`

---

## Branching model

```
main          ← production-ready only; tagged releases
  └── dev     ← integration; all feature branches merge here first
        ├── feat/lang-switcher
        ├── fix/form-validation
        ├── chore/upgrade-tailwind
        └── client/muster-sanitaer   ← per-client forks of the template
```

- `main` is protected — no direct pushes, PR required, must pass CI.
- `dev` is the integration target — agents open PRs to `dev`, not `main`.
- `main` ← `dev` merges are done by the Git Workflow Master after QA.
- Client deployments live on `client/<slug>` branches, rebased on `main` at release time.

### Commit message format (Conventional Commits)

```
<type>(<scope>): <short description>

# Types: feat | fix | chore | refactor | style | docs | test
# Scope: optional, matches the primary file/area changed
#
# Examples:
# feat(ui): add TestimonialsSection component
# fix(form): correct WhatsApp number encoding
# chore(deps): upgrade SvelteKit to 2.58
# refactor(config): extract OPENING_HOURS to config.ts
```

- Subject line ≤ 72 characters, imperative mood, no period.
- Body (optional) explains *why*, not *what*.

---

## Hard limits — things agents must never do

- Do not switch the adapter away from `adapter-node` (no `adapter-vercel`, `adapter-auto`, etc.).
- Do not add `vercel.json` or `vercel.ts` — this project deploys to Hetzner/Coolify.
- Do not install an i18n library (`svelte-i18n`, `paraglide`) — `i18n.ts` is intentionally minimal.
- Do not add state management libraries (Pinia, Zustand, Jotai) — use Svelte 5 runes.
- Do not commit `.env.local` or any real credentials.
- Do not introduce `any` types without a `// eslint-disable` comment and justification.
- Do not push directly to `main`.
